ed. Captain Anne Reed read them the articles, including the added one. They cheered, the way crews do. Pirates are sentimentalists. It's why they survive.\n\nA year later, a new a brass astrolabe surfaced — they always do — and Captain Anne Reed was packed before the ink dried. the quartermaster closed the tavern for 'renovations' and came along, because that's what friends do.\n\nPort Royal shrank astern again, beloved and boring in the best way. Ahead: a brass astrolabe, the sea, the test. Captain Anne Reed stood at the wheel and felt the old lift. This is the life."}]}

